            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The logic behind diagnostic blocks is very straightforward. What has not been determined is the way diagnostic blocks can be best used.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Philosophical essay.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The interventional pain management physician would serve as the diagnostic expert by efficiently determining the source of the patient's pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">&quot;The Best Likelihood Scenario&quot; might improve diagnostic accuracy while decreasing societal costs.</AbstractText>
